id: pm-glossary-yrza
title: "SDK gap: protected extension envelopes need native cost and producer cursor controls"
description: "Release blocker for the exact native output-control contract. Published SDK CommandDefinition.read_output only opts read-only handlers into host shaping; validateReadOutputOptions runs before parser overrides and refuses mutation cost flags. Native output cursors are decoded and applied outside the handler, so producer-owned pagination is applied twice. No public consume-cursor or mutation-envelope capability exists in ExtensionCommandSdk. Public declarations and open upstream searches were checked; no matching open issue was found. Upstream issue creation is outside this task. The package uses explicit budget and cursor fallback flags without shadowing native flags or misdeclaring writes as reads."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: release-blocker,sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli"
created_at: "2026-11-05T11:51:59.773Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T11:55:22.486Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Upstream provides truthful mutation cost controls and producer-owned native cursor consumption; native flags pass packed npm and Bun write and multi-page journeys without generic witness compaction; remove documented fallback limitation only after those exact host gates pass
parent: pm-glossary-gjws
